# Store every text file with LF in the repository, whatever the machine that committed it.
#
# This project is developed on Windows, where git's autocrlf turns LF into CRLF on checkout. Left
# alone, that is harmless locally and produces whole file diffs the day someone commits from macOS
# or Linux. Normalising here settles it once.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures whose exact bytes are the point. The legacy export is parsed by tools/convert-legacy.ts, and
# the session file is read by Playwright: neither should be rewritten by a line ending rule.
*.png binary
selftest/fake-session.json -text

# Windows launcher. cmd.exe misreads blocks and labels in a batch file with LF endings, so this
# one keeps CRLF in the working tree whatever the rule above says.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
